## Review checklist for Dushich / Aria
  [ ] Heal logic performs the same actions, in the same order, at the same
        cadence (only the if/else shape changed to compute a shared `healthy` flag).
  [ ] `set -euo pipefail` safety: all arithmetic is in assignments or `if`
        conditions (no bare `((...))` statements that could trip -e).
  [ ] journald capture: stdout only; verify with
        `systemctl restart noobia_wifi_guard && journalctl -u noobia_wifi_guard -f`
        (restart is a reviewed action — coordinate).
  [ ] No credentials, keys, or private data in any log line (verified: only
        interface name, profile name, static IP, and command outcome).

## Verification (after Aria/Dushich apply)
  1. `bash -n` the applied script (already passed for this proposal).
  2. With consent and in a controlled test window, force a degraded state
     (e.g. temporarily disable the AP SSID or unplug the dongle), and confirm:
     one `degraded (cycle 1)` line, one heartbeat per ~5 min, one `recovered`
     line when the link returns.
  3. `journalctl -u noobia_wifi_guard --since "-10 min"` reads as expected.

## Rollback
Restore the previous script (kept verbatim in section 1 and in Git history
at b46f42b), then `systemctl restart noobia_wifi_guard`. The logging adds no
persistent state; there is nothing to migrate.
